{"body": "While fixing some issues on the PyIceberg ends to fully support UUIDs: apache/iceberg-python#2007\nI noticed this issue, and was suprised since UUID used to work with Spark, but it turns out that the dictionary encoded UUID was not implemented yet.\nFor PyIceberg we only generate little data, so therefore this wasn't caught previously.\nCloses #4581", "date": "2025-06-16T11:35:25Z", "hash": "sha256:6dfd256ad2ae2762c3d2", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#13324", "meta": {"additions": 43, "base": "main", "closed_at": "2025-07-09T22:29:16Z", "closes": [4581], "comments": 6, "deletions": 2, "draft": false, "files": ["arrow/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/arrow/vectorized/GenericArrowVectorAccessorFactory.java", "spark/v3.5/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/data/vectorized/ArrowVectorAccessorFactory.java", "spark/v3.5/spark/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/data/vectorized/parquet/TestParquetVectorizedReads.java"], "labels": ["spark", "arrow"], "merged_at": "2025-07-09T22:29:16Z", "merged_by": "Fokko", "n_files": 3, "number": 13324, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "reviews": [{"at": "2025-06-17T03:59:34Z", "by": "kevinjqliu", "state": "APPROVED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T02:26:13Z", "by": "dingo4dev", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-07-08T20:51:06Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-07-08T20:51:32Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "APPROVED"}, {"at": "2025-07-09T22:25:31Z", "by": "Fokko", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-07-09T22:29:11Z", "by": "Fokko", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-07-09T23:56:50Z", "by": "liamzwbao", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-07-16T18:23:57Z", "by": "Fokko", "state": "COMMENTED"}], "state": "merged", "thumbs_up": 0, "updated_at": "2025-07-16T18:23:57Z"}, "people": ["Fokko"], "refs": ["gh:apache/iceberg-python#2007", "gh:apache/iceberg#4581", "gh:apache/iceberg#4581"], "source": "github", "title": "Spark: Support Parquet dictionary encoded UUIDs", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/13324"}
{"body": "Spark has insert-replace-where query  since version 3.5.\nCurrent Iceberg only has metadata-level support, this pr will contribute a row-level support.\nIf table could use metadata to achieve the insert-replace-where, then will keep the original overwrite logical plan.\nOriginal logical plan is\n== Analyzed Logical Plan ==\nOverwriteByExpression RelationV2[name#141, age#142, job#143] spark_catalog.aorakili.person spark_catalog.aorakili.person, (age#142 > 22), false\n+- Project [cast(col1#144 as string) AS name#147, cast(col2#145 as int) AS age#148, cast(col3#146 as string) AS job#149]\n   +- LocalRelation [col1#144, col2#145, col3#146]\n\nFor Copy-On-Write mode, the logical plan is\n== Optimized Logical Plan ==\nReplaceData RelationV2[name#13, age#14, job#15] spark_catalog.aorakili.person spark_catalog.aorakili.person, IcebergWrite(table=spark_catalog.aorakili.person, format=PARQUET)\n+- Union false, false\n   :- Project [name#13, age#14, job#15]\n   :  +- Filter (dynamicpruningexpression(_file#24 IN (list#43 [])) AND NOT ((age#14 > 22) <=> true))\n   :     :  +- Aggregate [_file#42], [_file#42]\n   :     :     +- Project [_file#42]\n   :     :        +- Filter (isnotnull(age#40) AND (age#40 > 22))\n   :     :           +- RelationV2[age#40, _file#42] spark_catalog.aorakili.person\n   :     +- RelationV2[name#13, age#14, job#15, _file#24] spark_catalog.aorakili.person\n   +- Expand [[name#19, age#20, job#21]], [name#27, age#28, job#29]\n      +- LocalRelation [name#19, age#20, job#21]\n\nFor Merge-On-Read mode, the logical plan is\n== Optimized Logical Plan ==\nWriteDelta RelationV2[name#54, age#55, job#56] spark_catalog.aorakili.person spark_catalog.aorakili.person, org.apache.iceberg.spark.source.SparkPositionDeltaWrite@77d5395a\n+- RebalancePartitions [_spec_id#75, _partition#76, _file#73], 402653184\n   +- Union false, false\n      :- Expand [[1, null, null, null, _file#65, _pos#66L, _spec_id#63, _partition#64]], [__row_operation#69, name#70, age#71, job#72, _file#73, _pos#74L, _spec_id#75, _partition#76]\n      :  +- Project [_file#65, _pos#66L, _spec_id#63, _partition#64]\n      :     +- Filter (isnotnull(age#55) AND (age#55 > 22))\n      :        +- RelationV2[age#55, _file#65, _pos#66L, _spec_id#63, _partition#64] spark_catalog.aorakili.person\n      +- Expand [[3, name#60, age#61, job#62, null, null, null, null]], [__row_operation#78, name#79, age#80, job#81, _file#82, _pos#83L, _spec_id#84, _partition#85]\n         +- LocalRelation [name#60, age#61, job#62]", "date": "2025-06-17T09:35:06Z", "hash": "sha256:71dbb1727ab6984a11c7", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#13332", "meta": {"additions": 479, "base": "main", "closed_at": "2025-07-26T00:18:27Z", "comments": 2, "deletions": 2, "draft": false, "files": ["spark/v3.5/spark-extensions/src/main/scala/org/apache/iceberg/spark/extensions/IcebergSparkSessionExtensions.scala", "spark/v3.5/spark-extensions/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/catalyst/optimizer/RewriteInsertReplaceWhere.scala", "spark/v3.5/spark-extensions/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/extensions/TestCopyOnWriteReplaceWhere.java", "spark/v3.5/spark-extensions/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/extensions/TestMergeOnReadReplaceWhere.java", "spark/v3.5/spark-extensions/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/extensions/TestReplaceWhere.java", "spark/v3.5/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/SparkTable.java", "spark/v3.5/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/SparkWrite.java"], "labels": ["spark", "stale"], "n_files": 7, "number": 13332, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "state": "closed", "thumbs_up": 0, "updated_at": "2025-07-26T00:18:27Z"}, "people": ["dolcino-li"], "refs": [], "source": "github", "title": "Spark3.5: Support ROW level operation on insert-replace-where", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/13332"}
{"body": "Summary\nFixes an issue where retry flag was-retried was not accessible after request execution due to context isolation.\nPreviously, requests were executed with a BasicHttpContext instance, which caused Apache HttpClient to create internal child contexts. As a result, any attributes (such as was-retried) set during the retry process were not visible to the caller after the response.\nThis change ensures that a shared HttpClientContext is used when executing requests, allowing retry-related attribute to persist and be accessible for error handling and observability.\nPrior work: #12818\nChanges\nUse HttpClientContext.create() instead of BasicHttpContext.\nTesting\nAdding a unit test that simulates a self-conflict table corruption scenario.", "date": "2025-06-18T02:12:12Z", "hash": "sha256:4d2293cc1e6957dbfe4d", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#13339", "meta": {"additions": 72, "base": "main", "closed_at": "2025-07-25T06:07:35Z", "comments": 10, "deletions": 11, "draft": false, "files": ["core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/HTTPClient.java", "core/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/TestHTTPClient.java"], "labels": ["core", "stale"], "n_files": 2, "number": 13339, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "reviews": [{"at": "2025-06-18T02:13:22Z", "by": "singhpk234", "state": "APPROVED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T04:37:16Z", "by": "singhpk234", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T04:54:08Z", "by": "singhpk234", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T05:05:34Z", "by": "XJDKC", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T05:40:32Z", "by": "singhpk234", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T15:49:26Z", "by": "XJDKC", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T15:49:53Z", "by": "singhpk234", "state": "APPROVED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T15:52:39Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T16:05:49Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T16:08:01Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T16:09:57Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T16:10:50Z", "by": "RussellSpitzer", "state": "APPROVED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T17:18:50Z", "by": "XJDKC", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T17:19:41Z", "by": "XJDKC", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-06-18T17:25:08Z", "by": "XJDKC", "state": "COMMENTED"}], "state": "closed", "thumbs_up": 1, "updated_at": "2025-07-25T06:07:35Z"}, "people": ["XJDKC"], "refs": ["gh:apache/iceberg#12818"], "source": "github", "title": "Core: Use Shared HttpClientContext to Persist \"was-retried\" Attribute", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/13339"}
